  "market_context": "Late-night US30 downtrend with cascading price drops, followed by loss of momentum and consolidation near a market bottom. Analyst observed RSI forming higher lows while price made lower lows, signaling bullish divergence.",
  "key_observation": "RSI formed multiple consecutive higher lows while price made lower lows, culminating in RSI breaking above 50—confirming bullish momentum shift—and triggering two long scalp entries at 32,372 and 32,417.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a late-night cascading downtrend in US30, then noted loss of momentum and consolidation phase.",
    "Step 2: Plotted 21, 50, and 200 MAs to confirm price trading below all three during the dump.",
    "Step 3: Observed RSI forming repeated higher lows while price made lower lows—initially dismissed early divergence as non-tradeable.",
    "Step 4: Waited for extremely clear RSI divergence: five consecutive higher lows, then RSI crossing above 50 to confirm bullish momentum.",
    "Step 5: Entered first long at 32,372 on 1-minute chart after strong rejection wick and RSI confirmation.",
    "Step 6: Entered second long at 32,417 on 1-minute chart after another rejection wick and confluence with prior analysis on 15-minute chart.",
    "Step 7: Set take-profit near 21 MA at ~32,498 (two dollars below round number 32,500), using small 0.02 lot size for scalping."
  ],
  "outcome": "Two trades: +$251.78 and +$161.22 (total $403.36) on 0.02 lot size; both closed before major rally to 32,798.",
  "lessons": "Wait for *extremely clear* RSI divergence (multiple higher lows + RSI >50) before entering; use HTF (15M) for structure, LTF (1M) for sniper entries; scalp small moves with tight R:R rather than chasing extended rallies.",
